==English==
{{rfi}}
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikispecies|Allium fistulosum}}
===Alternative forms===
* [[scullion]]

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno|en}} ''[[scalun]]'' (cognate with Old French ''[[escalogne]]''), from a Proto-Romance derivation of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|Ascalonius||lang=la}} (in ''{{term|caepa|lang=la||onion}} Ascalonius'', "shallot"), from {{term|Ascalo|lang=la||Ascalon}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Ἀσκάλων||tr=Askalon|lang=grc|[[w:Ashkelon|Ascalon]], an ancient Palestinian port}}, from {{etyl|phn|en}} {{rfscript|phn|sc=Phnx}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈskæ.lɪ.ən]|[ˈskæ.ljn̩]|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|now|chiefly|US|lang=en}} A [[spring onion]], ''[[Allium fistulosum]]''.
# {{context|now|chiefly|US|lang=en}} Any of various similar members of the [[genus]] ''[[Allium]]''.
# Any onion that lacks a fully developed [[bulb]].
# {{context|US|Scotland|lang=en}} A [[leek]].

====Synonyms====
{{checksense}}
* [[spring onion]]
* [[green onion]]

